  "label_noise_notes": [
    "Train boxes were drawn by a single radiologist per image (Shih et al. 2019); the Kaggle test was read by three and merged by intersection, so official test boxes are smaller. Our val/test come from the single-read train pool: no train/test reader shift internally, but the labels are themselves noisy.",
    "About 2,500 triple-read images (stage-1 test + 1,500 others) are mixed into stage-2 train and cannot be identified.",
    "'No Lung Opacity / Not Normal' (other abnormalities) is target=0: hard negatives that look abnormal; boxes exist only for 'Lung Opacity'.",
    "Box extents are subjective (opacity boundaries are diffuse): L1-trained boxes tend to be too large; top Kaggle teams shrank predicted boxes by ~12-17%.",
    "stage_2_detailed_class_info.csv has 3,543 duplicate rows (removed); no conflicting class/target labels.",
    "PatientAge has 5 values > 100 (header errors); kept raw in metadata, bucketed as 'invalid' here.",
    "Source NIH labels (orig_labels / subset_init_label in the mapping JSON) are NLP-mined and must not be used as features."
  ]
